WEBVTT

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.418
Who gets everything you own?

00:00:02.618 --> 00:00:06.002
If you don’t have a will in Ontario, the law decides for you.

00:00:07.052 --> 00:00:14.310
Without a will, a married spouse gets the first $350,000, then shares the rest with your children.

00:00:14.510 --> 00:00:17.451
A common-law partner gets nothing automatically.

00:00:18.501 --> 00:00:19.927
With a will, you choose.

00:00:20.127 --> 00:00:23.016
Who gets your home, your savings and your belongings.

00:00:23.216 --> 00:00:26.068
Who handles it all, and who cares for your children.

00:00:27.118 --> 00:00:30.160
Powers of attorney name who acts for you if you can’t.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:33.907
One for your money and property, and one for your personal care.

00:00:34.957 --> 00:00:37.002
You sign in front of two witnesses.

00:00:37.202 --> 00:00:41.650
Or by video, when one witness is a licensed lawyer or paralegal.

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:45.254
With Titled, it takes two minutes to start.

00:00:45.454 --> 00:00:50.054
A partner lawyer calls you, and confirms a fixed fee before any work begins.

00:00:50.254 --> 00:00:53.824
Whether you own a home with others, or just want things in order.
